# AveroNova Definition of Done

A feature is DONE only when its complete real-world E2E acceptance test passes.

Never report DONE, READY, COMPLETE, or PASS because code compiles, a build/APK succeeds, unit code exists, UI appears, or an API endpoint exists.

## Status vocabulary (use only these)

- **IMPLEMENTED**: code exists
- **BUILT**: project compiles
- **TESTED**: a test was actually executed
- **VERIFIED**: expected result was confirmed
- **NOT VERIFIED**: required test could not be executed (environment limitation). Do not report PASS.
- **FAILED**: test ran and expected behavior failed
- **DONE**: all mandatory E2E acceptance tests passed

Distinguish Implementation / Build / APK / Runtime / E2E. If Runtime or E2E fails, final status is **NOT DONE**.

## Never say DONE if

- APK was not launched, API not tested, or DB effect not verified
- Offline, online recovery, or sync was not tested
- An old APK was tested, BrowserStack could not reach the required API, or a required platform was skipped
- There is an unresolved crash, or the result was only inferred from code

## Working vs verified

```
Implementation: PASS
Build: PASS
APK: PASS
Runtime: FAIL
E2E: FAIL
Final: NOT DONE
```

If a test cannot run due to environment limits, report **NOT VERIFIED**, never PASS.
